          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em concrete category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            that looks like a category of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+sets"} structured sets
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#with_a_family_of_collection_of_elements With a family of collection of elements
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with a type of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C)
              and for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:Ob(C)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:Ob(C)
              a set of morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mor
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor_C(a, b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %strong concrete category
              if for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:Ob(C)
              there is a set of elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(a)
              and for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:Ob(C)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:Ob(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi Mor
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_{a,b} \colon Mor_C(a,b) \to (U(a) \to U(b))
          %h3#with_one_collection_of_elements With one collection of elements
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with a type of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C)
              and a set of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
              with source and target functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:Mor(C) \to Ob(C)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t:Mor(C) \to Ob(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %strong concrete category
              if there is a set of elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(C)
              with a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o:U(C) \to Ob(C)
              with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:Mor(C) \to Func(Set)
              (and functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi Set
                    %mo :
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_{Set}:Func(Set) \to U(C)
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi Set
                      %mo :
                      %mi Func
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_{Set}:Func(Set) \to U(C)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:Mor(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(f) = o(s_{Set}(i(f)))
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = o(t_{Set}(i(f)))
          %h3#with_a_functor_into_set With a functor into Set
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong concrete category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U : C \to Set
            %p
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %em concretizable
              if and only if it admits a faithful functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: C \to Set
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Very often it is useful to consider the case where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              by some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_0 \in C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \simeq C(c_0,-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dualities
              induced by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+adjunctions"} dual adjunctions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, U: C \to Set)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %em representably concrete
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_0
              is then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
              of the category.
            %p
              We remark that the existence of a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: C \to Set
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is representable by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              or even just
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has a left adjoint.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              One can also consider concrete categories over any base category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              instead of necessarily over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AdámekHerrlichStrecker90"} Adámek, Herrlich &amp; Strecker 1990
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat(X)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              A concrete category is
              %strong univalent
              if its underlying category (by forgetting the functor into
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              Any small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              can be made into a concrete category by setting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X)
              to be the set of all arrows with codomain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X \to Y)
              given by composition with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
          %p The following furnish examples of concrete categories, with the first three representably concrete:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Set
                itself with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_0 = \{\bullet\}
                the singleton set.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Top
                with the separator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_0
                taken to be the one-point space.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: C \to Set
                is faithful (because it preserves equalizers and reflects isomorphisms) and has a left adjoint. As special cases, we have the usual collection of examples of concrete categories:
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
          %p A category may be concretizable in more than one way:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Take
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                to be the category of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+space"} Banach space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                (so
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi T
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \| T v \| \leq \| v \|
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                in the source). Then there are two versions of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                that one may use: one where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U ( V )
                (for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                a Banach space) consists of
                %em every
                vector in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U ( V )
                consists of those vectors bounded by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                (so the closed unit ball in
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %li
              %p
                Insofar as categories such as
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Vect
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separators"} separators
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k
                may be
                %em monadic
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                in many different ways. For example, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is
                = succeed "-dimensional," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(V, -): Vect_k \to Set
                is monadic and realizes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k
                as equivalent to the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                over the matrix algebra
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(V, V)
            %li
              %p
                Any Grothendieck topos is concretizable, but not necessarily (and typically not) representably concretizable. If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = Sh(C, J)
                is the category of sheaves on a small site
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, J)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi monadic
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 0
                      %mi Set
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C, J) \hookrightarrow Set^{C^{op}} \stackrel{monadic}{\to} Set/C_0 \stackrel{\Sigma_{C_0}}{\to} Set.
              %p
                But if for example
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                is the category of sheaves over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                can serve as a single separator of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \stackrel{\to}{\to} Z
                whenever the support of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                is strictly contained in the support of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                A concrete category that is equipped with the structure of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                in a compatible way is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+site"} concrete site
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaves"} concrete sheaves
                on a concrete site is concrete.
          %p
            Many familiar examples of “sets with additional structure” provide examples of concrete categories where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the usual ‘underlying set’:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mon
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
                and monoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
                and abelian group homomorphisms is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                Given a commutative ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
                of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                and
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
                is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                Given a commutative ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Alg
                of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras"} algebras
                and
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CRing
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
                and commutative ring homomorphisms is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Field
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Field
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
                and field homomorphisms is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi HeytAlg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HeytAlg
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebras"} Heyting algebras
                and Heyting algebra homomorphisms is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Frm
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Frm
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frames"} frames
                and frame homomorphisms is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Conv
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conv
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+spaces"} convergence spaces
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                and continuous functions is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Met
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
                is a concrete category.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi StrictCat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StrictCat
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+functors"} strict functors
                is a concrete category.
          %p
            There are other examples of concretizable categories where the objects are described as sets, but one cannot choose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            satisfying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X) = X
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Set
                        %mo ⊥
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_\bot
                of sets and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+functions"} partial functions
                is a concrete category when equipped with the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⨿
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X) = X \amalg \{ * \}
                that adds a disjoint point, and sends a partial function to the total function whose undefined values are set to the point.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rel
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel
                of sets and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
                has a separator given by the singleton set. Thus, it is a concrete category when equipped with the functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi PowerSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X) = PowerSet(X)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X \to Y)
                given by composition of relations (viewing a subset of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                as a relation on
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Rel
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi \in Rel(X, Y)
                we have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \in \Phi
                iff
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in \Phi \circ \{x\}
          %h2#nonexamples Non-examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                is
                %em not
                concretizable
            %li
              %p
                The opposite category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
                equipped with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+spectrum"} prime spectrum
                functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op} \to Set
                is not concrete, since the prime spectrum is not faithful. This is one of the reasons for the use of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Prefunc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prefunc
                of sets and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prefunctions"} prefunctions
                is not a concrete category.
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is concretizable (since it fully and faithfully embeds in the concrete category
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is concretizable, so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By assumption, there is a faithful functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi op
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{op}: C^{op} \to Set^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, \mathbf{2}): Set^{op} \to Set
              is monadic.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Of course, since a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              may possess a separator but no
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coseparator"} coseparator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
              is representably concrete if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is.
          %h3#morphism_evaluation_and_extensionality Morphism evaluation and extensionality
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              In any concrete category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, U:C \to Set)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)((-))\colon Hom(a,b) \times U(a) \to U(b)
            %p
              such that for every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon Hom(a,b)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Mor
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon Mor_C(b,c)
              and every element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:U(a)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g \circ f)(x) = g(f(x))
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_A(x) = x
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Because
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} currying
              the injective function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{a,b}
              of the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              means that there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)((-))\colon Hom(a,b) \times U(a) \to U(b)
              which satisfies the above axioms.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              In any concrete category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, U:C \to Set)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
              with respect to the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon Hom(A,B)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon Hom(A,B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = g(x)
              for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon El(A)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1} \to U(a)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(a)
          %h3#relationship_with_wellpointedness Relationship with well-pointedness
          %p
            The category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of sets and functions is both concrete and well-pointed. However, not every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed category
            is an concrete category, as well-pointed categories are not required to be
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+categories"} concrete categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            aren’t defined to be concrete. Moreover, not every concrete category is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Field
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            and field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            is concrete, but is not well-pointed because it doesn’t have a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %p
            The distinction between concreteness and well-pointedness is the distinction between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+elements"} global elements
            in a concrete category with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %h3#characterization Characterization
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
              is concretizable, i.e., admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              The “only if”-part is due to
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Isbell63"} Isbell 1963
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C\to D
              is a faithful functor, then it is injective on equivalence classes of regular subobjects. For suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\colon a \to x
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\colon x\rightrightarrows y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\colon b\to x
              is the equalizer of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,k\colon x\rightrightarrows z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a) \cong F(b)
              as subobjects of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f m = g m
              and so
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(f)\circ F(m) = F(g)\circ F(m)
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(f)\circ F(n) = F(g)\circ F(n)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is faithful)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f n = g n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\cong b
              as subobjects of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              is regularly well-powered, it follows that any category admitting a faithful functor to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              must also be so.
            %p (Actually, Isbell proved a more general condition which applies to categories that may lack finite limits.)
            %p
              “If” was proven in (
              %a{:href => "#Freyd"}> Freyd
              ). The argument is rather more involved, passing through
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+categories"} additive categories
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              A relatively deep application of Isbell’s result is that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is
              %em not
              concretizable, even though it is a quotient of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              which
              %em is
              concretizable. (
              %a{:href => "#Freyd70"}> Freyd 70
              )
            %p
              A similar way to use Isbell’s result applies to show that a really vast number of model categories can not have a concrete localization at weak equivalences: see
              %a{:href => "#DiliLore"} Di Liberti and Loregian, 2017
